@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: siege is taught by playing a gated siege, not by a slide that describes one
' status: proposed 2026-09-17, not implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
' would touch: not in this tree — no tutorial runner or siege mode exists under
'   the sandbox checkout (measured 2026-09-17). Locate the owning tutorial
'   module before a covers: line can be honest.
'   the lines this mode is made of .... _spec/_plans/tutorial-siege-lines.puml
'   ships if they take part ........... _spec/_plans/tutorial-ships.puml
'   turn-21 prep as a later beat ...... _spec/_plans/tutorial-turn-21-prep.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE LINE ITEM SETTLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' "interactive siege mode" is a TUTORIAL SHAPE. The player acts inside a siege,
' with gates, not a film of one. The engine's siege rules are the teacher; the
' tutorial only sequences which verbs are unlocked.
'
' ── WHAT IT DOES NOT SETTLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   win condition of a siege (lines, ships, clock, king)
'   how many beats, and whether skip exists
'   whether this is a mode flag on the engine or a scripted match
'
' A scripted match that bypasses the engine will teach a siege the live game
' does not play. The tutorial issues legal moves in a real siege, or it is a
' slide with extra buttons.
title PLANNED — siege tutorial is a gated real siege;\nnot a slide that describes one

component "siege rules (engine)" as RULE <<app>>
component "tutorial gates\nwhich verbs are live" as GATE <<app>>
component "the player acts" as PLAY <<app>>
component "**a film of a siege**\nno legal move is issued" as SLIDE <<error>>
component "siege lines beat" as LINES <<app>>
component "ships beat (if in siege)" as SHIP <<app>>

RULE ARROW_MAIN GATE
GATE ARROW_MAIN PLAY
PLAY ARROW_MAIN RULE : legal moves only
SLIDE ARROW_ERROR PLAY : buttons that do not\nhit the engine
LINES ARROW_MAIN GATE
SHIP ARROW_OPTIONAL GATE

note bottom of SLIDE
  **Description is not interactive mode, because a
  caption over an idle engine teaches the wrong
  activity.** Every beat must submit a legal
  action the live rules already accept.
end note

note bottom of GATE
  **Gates unlock verbs rather than outcomes, so
  ships may remain hidden until siege lines are
  placed.** The tutorial nevertheless may not
  force a victory the engine would refuse.
end note

note right of RULE
  **Siege has two owners: line and ship lessons
  are separate plans because each is a distinct
  tutorial beat.** This file owns only the runner
  that sequences those beats against live rules.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in**
  ==
  **1. Name live siege.** What starts it, what ends it, which pieces may act.
  If that contract is fuzzy, write tutorial-siege-lines.puml first — a runner
  with no line rule is a slide.
  --
  **2. Build the runner as a gated match.** Same engine, restricted verb set,
  fail-closed if the player issues an out-of-beat move. No skip that writes
  a won siege without play.
  ==
  **3. Drop beats in, one plan each.** Lines, then ships if they belong, then
  turn-21 prep. Interactive mode is done when those beats run inside it, not
  when a menu row exists.
  --
  **Left open**: skip; whether ranked play can enter this mode; how failure
  retries a beat without resetting the board illegally.
end legend
@enduml
